--TEST--
`->$name` and `->{expr}` over an operand that is no property key are `E0235` in every position a member is named — read, write, call and `?->` — reported by the checker, per `rule:classes/no-dynamic-properties` and `rule:types/property-key-access`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Box {
    public string $name = "a";
    public function label(): string { return "l"; }
}
var $b = new Box();
string $n = "name";
// `rule:types/property-key-access` moved this refusal out of the parser, because the operand's
// *type* is what decides it now: a plain `string` names a member only when
// the statement runs, and there is nothing to resolve it against.
echo $b->$n, "\n";
// `->{expr}` is the same construct written the other way, and the caret sits
// on the operand rather than on the braces because the type is the question.
$b->{$n} = "z";
// A computed *method* name is refused for `rule:classes/no-call-magic`'s older reason —
// dispatch is not computed at all — so no operand type would admit it.
echo $b->{"lab" . "el"}(), "\n";
// `?->` changes only whether the receiver is tested, never how the
// member is named.
echo $b?->$n, "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:11:10
   |
11 | echo $b->$n, "\n";
   |          ^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: `rule:types/property-key-access` admits `$obj->$key` only where `$key` is a `property<T>` the receiver satisfies — convert the name with `as property<ClassName>`, where the set it may hold is checked, or write the member out; data whose keys are only known at run time belongs in an `array<T>`, whose keys are `string`

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:14:6
   |
14 | $b->{$n} = "z";
   |      ^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: `rule:types/property-key-access` admits `$obj->$key` only where `$key` is a `property<T>` the receiver satisfies — convert the name with `as property<ClassName>`, where the set it may hold is checked, or write the member out; data whose keys are only known at run time belongs in an `array<T>`, whose keys are `string`

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:17:11
   |
17 | echo $b->{"lab" . "el"}(), "\n";
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: `rule:classes/no-call-magic` refuses a computed *dispatch* itself rather than its spelling, and `rule:types/property-key`'s `property<T>` names a property rather than a method — write the call out, or `match` on the name and call each arm

error[E0235]: a member name cannot be computed (`->$name` / `->{expr}`)
   --> %s:20:11
   |
20 | echo $b?->$n, "\n";
   |           ^^ this names a member only when the statement runs
   = help: `rule:types/property-key-access` admits `$obj->$key` only where `$key` is a `property<T>` the receiver satisfies — convert the name with `as property<ClassName>`, where the set it may hold is checked, or write the member out; data whose keys are only known at run time belongs in an `array<T>`, whose keys are `string`

